{
  "dom_id": "step-q327649",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Last year, a factory produced $800$ bicycles. This year, production is $150%$ greater than last year. How many bicycles did the factory produce this year?\n\nThe factory produced\n{{field-1}}\nbicycles this year.",
  "worked_solution": "To find this year's bicycle production, we apply a $150%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $150%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+150%=250%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n250%=\\frac{250}{100}=2.5\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $2.5:$\n\n$$\n800\\times 2.5=2,000\n$$\n\nSo, the factory produced $2000$ bicycles this year.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
